Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 12 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 2, row A9): B1896'S LOCK HOLDS ITS VERDICT LINE
 BY ITS SENTENCES, AND A ROW BY THE GATE THE RUN NAMES

A reader's check of main's answers at Review 80 (agy-002's; row A9, not checked by main): as with B1893's
lock, main did not make the reader's own plants. The reader's passes, in main's words: the verdict line
changed after the part the lock holds, and the gates named for two rows replaced on the page.

Made again here, in a scratch checkout, on the commit before this patch. The lock held the verdict line by
its first 106 characters, of 2,843:
  - "17 OF MAIN'S 22" turned into "22 OF MAIN'S 22": the lock PASSES;
  - "FIVE PASS" turned into "NONE PASSES": PASSES;
  - the whole line replaced after the part held: FAILS, by another test, as the builder made it;
  - the gates named for two rows replaced by another gate's name: FAILS, as the builder made it. With the
    run's gate kept after the other's name, the row passes what the lock asked.

The lock now holds the verdict line by six of its sentences, holds that their numbers are the runs' (17 of
22 caught, five that pass, three of the five written after reading), and asks that a row of a caught case
open its answer with a gate the run names for it. Five planted changes pass what the lock asked of the
verdict before and are reported now. On the patch, in a scratch checkout, the three passes above FAIL.

When the fifth series of the enforcement package lands, one of the five that pass is closed, and this
lock's own test of them says so by design; the sentences held here change with it, and that is main's.

The lock passes: 9 tests. Not checked by main. Tested against planted errors by the session that wrote it.
